From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Flysoft <flysoftbeta@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 02:45:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rb: shared D3D11 fence capture hand-off (deliver at submit,
 GPU-side wait)

Remote mode only (kRbSharedFence pools, negotiated): viz signals a shared
fence on the Graphite D3D11 writer right after the capture copy is submitted
and delivers the frame immediately with {fence token, value, adapter LUID}
instead of waiting for the CPU completion callback (which waited for the next
present, ~12.8 ms). The endpoint waits on the GPU (ID3D11DeviceContext4::Wait)
before VPP/encode and returns consumed=true after its source read completes,
which gates Done()/pool reuse. Keyed-mutex pools remain the fallback.
Measured (research/m4/fence-impl.md): Viz capture 14.8 -> 1.3 ms P50,
capture->decoded -10 to -13 ms in every pair.

Patch-Name: 19-rb-shared-fence

